Upstream-Status: Pending

dsDisplay: use intptr_t for display event callback handle

On LP64 (qemux86-64), intptr_t is long while int is 32-bit. devicesettings
implements _dsDisplayEventCallback with intptr_t, matching
dsRegisterDisplayEventCallback(intptr_t, ...). The typedef still used int.

---
 include/dsDisplay.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/dsDisplay.h b/include/dsDisplay.h
--- a/include/dsDisplay.h
+++ b/include/dsDisplay.h
@@ -121,7 +121,7 @@
  *
  * @pre dsRegisterDisplayEventCallback()
  */
-typedef void (*dsDisplayEventCallback_t)(int handle, dsDisplayEvent_t event,
+typedef void (*dsDisplayEventCallback_t)(intptr_t handle, dsDisplayEvent_t event,
                                              void* eventData/*Optional*/);
 
 /**
